@@ -0,0 +1,34 @@
+# Conservative file transactions
+
+[Source: cli_files.py](cli_files.py)
+
+Lets initialization and synchronization prepare file changes, detect conflicts before writing, and undo their own writes after ordinary failures.
+
+## Responsibilities and collaborators
+
+Owns managed-path checks, bounded reads, immutable change plans and local file replacement.
+
+![Initializer change requests → Change plans + preflight → Filesystem / rollback](images/cli_files-flow.svg)
+
+Works directly with the standard library and filesystem; callers retain ownership of scope and authorization.
+
+## Interface and data
+
+`Conflict(ValueError)` reports unsafe or conflicting resources. Frozen `Change` carries root:Path, relative:Path, before:bytes|None, after:bytes|None and mode:int; its path property validates the destination. An absent after value requests deletion.
+
+| Callable or interface | Contract |
+| --- | --- |
+| `safe_path(root: Path, relative: str \| Path) -> Path` | Returns a Path after rejecting absolute/traversing relative names, symlinks and invalid intermediate directories. |
+| `read_bytes(path: Path) -> bytes \| None` | Returns file bytes or None when absent; rejects non-files and files above 4 MiB. |
+| `plan(root: Path, relative: str \| Path, data: bytes \| None, *, replace: bool=False, mode: int=420) -> Change \| None` | Returns Change or None for identical bytes. None plans deletion; existing content requires replace=True; existing permissions are retained. |
+| `atomic_replace(path: Path, data: bytes, mode: int) -> None` | Writes and fsyncs a temporary file, applies mode and atomically replaces the destination. |
+| `apply(changes: list[Change]) -> list[str]` | Preflights before-bytes, creates directories and returns written paths; rollback removes its exclusively created inode even after a partial write, preserves replacement inodes, and restores its own unchanged replacements/deletions. |
+
+## Effects and failure behavior
+
+Raises Conflict or filesystem errors. Deletions are preflighted and restored on ordinary rollback if still absent. Atomic replacement is per file; the group is not crash-safe or protected against hostile concurrent writers. Callers must have write authorization.
+New files are identified by device/inode immediately after exclusive creation. Stream setup failures close the descriptor; interrupted writes remove the owned partial file and roll back earlier changes. A different inode at the same path is preserved; same-inode concurrent edits remain outside the transaction guarantee.
+
+## Example
+
+Use `plan(root, 'notes.md', b'# Notes\n')`; pass its non-None result to `apply([change])`.

